% Daml patterns: a multiple-party agreement signed one party at a time
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of a Daml project, written by the Daml translator
% (InsurLE2/migration/daml) from its source (kept in sources/): each template a fluent keyed by
% the contract id, each create and choice an action, who may do what integrity constraints.
% The ids of the contracts a command creates are places of its action: the ledger assigns them, a scenario names them.
% Who may do what, as one permission per command: the Legal View (Misc > Legal View of This LPS Program).

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 4.

the actions are:
    *a party* creates the agreement *an agreement* with signatories list *a signatories list*; known as create_agreement.
    *a party* creates the pending *a pending* with final contract signatories list *a final contract signatories list* and already signed list *an already signed list*; known as create_pending.
    *a party* archives the agreement *an agreement*; known as archive_agreement.
    *a party* archives the pending *a pending*; known as archive_pending.

the fluents are:
    *an agreement* is an agreement with signatories list *a signatories list*; known as agreement.
    *a pending* is a pending with final contract signatories list *a final contract signatories list* and already signed list *an already signed list*; known as pending.

the knowledge base multiparty includes:

the text of "the source daml/MultiplePartyAgreement.daml" is at "sources/daml/MultiplePartyAgreement.daml".

the text of "the source daml/Utilities.daml" is at "sources/daml/Utilities.daml".

% Agreement: a party creates one; its signatories must be the one who submits (Daml's authorization)
when a party creates the agreement an agreement with signatories list a signatories list
then the agreement is an agreement with signatories list the signatories list.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the agreement an agreement with signatories list a signatories list
    and an element is in the signatories list
    and the element is different from the party.

% ensure of Agreement not stated: the condition `unique signatories` has no LE form here
it must not be true that
    a party creates the agreement an agreement with signatories list a signatories list
    and the agreement is an agreement with signatories list a second signatories list.

% Agreement: archiving one (Daml's Archive choice) is for its signatories, and it must be active
when a party archives the agreement an agreement
    and the agreement is an agreement with signatories list a signatories list
then it is not the case that the agreement is an agreement with signatories list the signatories list.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the agreement an agreement
    and the agreement is an agreement with signatories list a signatories list
    and an element is in the signatories list
    and the element is different from the party.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the agreement an agreement
    and it is not the case that the agreement is an agreement with signatories list a thing.

% Pending: a party creates one; its signatories must be the one who submits (Daml's authorization)
when a party creates the pending a pending with final contract signatories list a final contract signatories list and already signed list an already signed list
then the pending is a pending with final contract signatories list the final contract signatories list and already signed list the already signed list.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the pending a pending with final contract signatories list a final contract signatories list and already signed list an already signed list
    and an element is in the already signed list
    and the element is different from the party.

% ensure of Pending not stated: the condition `unique alreadySigned` has no LE form here
it must not be true that
    a party creates the pending a pending with final contract signatories list a final contract signatories list and already signed list an already signed list
    and the pending is a pending with final contract signatories list a second final contract signatories list and already signed list a second already signed list.

% Pending: archiving one (Daml's Archive choice) is for its signatories, and it must be active
when a party archives the pending a pending
    and the pending is a pending with final contract signatories list a final contract signatories list and already signed list an already signed list
then it is not the case that the pending is a pending with final contract signatories list the final contract signatories list and already signed list the already signed list.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the pending a pending
    and the pending is a pending with final contract signatories list a final contract signatories list and already signed list an already signed list
    and an element is in the already signed list
    and the element is different from the party.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the pending a pending
    and it is not the case that the pending is a pending with final contract signatories list a thing and already signed list a second thing.

% RESIDUE pending_sign BEGIN: choice Sign of Pending
